.card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; }

@container (inline-size > 30rem) {
  .card { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
}
```

Self-querying is forbidden by design: styles applied from inside `@container` could change the size the query just tested, and the layout would oscillate. Note that `container-type: size` would also need a definite block size, which is why `inline-size` is the usual choice.

